 to  him for comfort because i thought i  thought that i could  i think it's really um a continued  concern  that people are experiencing sexual  assault at such high rates there's no  reason why  we can't have great educational programs  run on campus  for young people in particular who are  by and large the ones on campus spaces  to kind of unpack some of the root  causes of gender-based violence and  sexual assault  cj's alleged assault happened in the  fall semester of 2018.  since then mount royal university has  made changes to its sexual assault  policy  the school's new president says its  procedures are more  trauma informed still he admits  there is likely more work to be done i  think the expectations of us are high  and we hate to disappoint and we are  going to continue to do what we can in  order to minimize these kinds of  incidents  but for cj life since the alleged  assaults has been difficult  she dropped out of school soon after her  sexual assault complaint was dismissed  and is now anxiously awaiting the  accused criminal charge to go  to trial she's also looking to the  future  hoping to one day return to  post-secondary school  it's going to be very very hard to trust  people  heather urex west global news calgary  decades of feeding the hungry next this  year's nobel peace prize winner  well we wanted to add a little levity to  your friday evening so  this is me a sea otter at a japanese  aquarium she's learned to  walk on her two hind legs i don't really  have much more to tell you about her  but sometimes no words are needed right  what a cutie well feeding the world's  hungry is what the world food program  has been doing for more than 50 years  it rarely makes headlines but its work  is so vital  as vital as it gets in fact it's kept  tens of millions of people in conflict  zones alive  and it's now being recognized with a  nobel peace prize  eric sorenson explains why  the setting was symbolic and fitting i  can't believe i'm in these  c